### Vertex AI in Firebase version 16.0.0
- Vertex AI in Firebase is now Generally Available (GA) and can
be used in production apps.

Use the Firebase AI Logic SDK to call the Vertex AI Gemini API
directly from your app. This client SDK is built specifically for use with
Android apps, offering security options against unauthorized clients
as well as integrations with other Firebase services.

 - If you're new to this library, visit the
 [getting started guide](https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-logic/get-started).

 - If you were using the preview version of the library, visit the
 [migration guide](https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-logic/migrate-from-preview) to learn
 about some important updates.
- **Breaking Change**: Changed `functionCallingConfig` parameter
type to be nullable in `ToolConfig`.
(GitHub [#6373](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6373))

- **Breaking Change**: Removed `functionResponse` accessor method
from `GenerateContentResponse`.
(GitHub [#6373](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6373))

- **Breaking Change**: Migrated `FirebaseVertexAIException` from a
sealed class to an abstract class, and marked constructors as internal.
(GitHub [#6368](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6368))

- Added support for `title` and `publicationDate` in citations.
(GitHub [#6309](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6309))

- Added support for `frequencyPenalty`, `presencePenalty`, and
`HarmBlockMethod`.
(GitHub [#6309](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6309))

- **Breaking Change**: Introduced `Citations` class. Now
`CitationMetadata` wraps that type.
(GitHub [#6276](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6276))

- **Breaking Change**: Reworked `Schema` declaration mechanism.
(GitHub [#6258](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6258))

- **Breaking Change**: Reworked function calling mechanism to use
the new `Schema` format. Function calls no longer use native types, nor
include references to the actual executable code.
(GitHub [#6258](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6258))

- **Breaking Change**: Made `totalBillableCharacters` field in
`CountTokens` nullable and optional.
(GitHub [#6294](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6294))

- **Breaking Change**: Removed `UNKNOWN` option for the
`HarmBlockThreshold` enum.
(GitHub [#6294](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6294))

- **Breaking Change**: Removed `UNSPECIFIED` option for the
`HarmBlockThreshold`, `HarmProbability`, `HarmSeverity`, and `BlockReason`
enums.
(GitHub [#6294](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6294))

- **Breaking Change**: Renamed `BlockThreshold` as
`HarmBlockThreshold`.
(GitHub [#6262](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6262))

- **Breaking Change**: Renamed all types and methods starting with
`blob` to start with `inlineData`.
(GitHub [#6309](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6309))

- **Breaking Change**: Changed the order of arguments in
`InlineDataPart` to match `ImagePart`.
(GitHub [#6340](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6340))

- **Breaking Change**: Changed `RequestOption` to accept only
`long` timeout values.
(GitHub [#6289](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6289))

- **Breaking Change**: Moved `requestOptions` to the last
positional argument in the `generativeModel` argument list.
(GitHub [#6292](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6292))

- **Breaking Change**: Replaced sealed classes with abstract
classes for `StringFormat`.
(GitHub [#6334](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6334))

- **Breaking Change**: Refactored enum classes to be normal
classes.
(GitHub [#6340](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6340))


### Vertex AI in Firebase version 16.0.0

- **Breaking Change**: Marked `GenerativeModel` properties as
private.
(GitHub [#6309](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/6309))

