### App Check version 17.0.0
- Added [`getLimitedUseAppCheckToken()`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/appcheck/FirebaseAppCheck#getLimitedUseAppCheckToken())
for obtaining limited-use tokens for protecting non-Firebase backends.

#### App Check Kotlin extensions version 17.0.0
The Kotlin extensions library transitively includes the updated
`firebase-appcheck` library. The Kotlin extensions library has no additional
updates.

### App Check Debug version 17.0.0
- Updated to keep App Check SDK versions aligned.

### App Check Debug Testing version 17.0.0
- Updated to keep App Check SDK versions aligned.

### App Check Play integrity version 17.0.0
- Updated to keep App Check SDK versions aligned.

### Authentication version 22.0.0
- **BREAKING CHANGE:** Removed SafetyNet support for app
verification during phone number authentication.

[App verification](https://firebase.google.com/docs/auth/android/phone-auth#enable-app-verification) will
now use [Play Integrity](https://developer.android.com/google/play/integrity)
by default, if available; otherwise, it falls back to reCAPTCHA.

- Added Firebase App Check support to Firebase Authentication.

- Migrated Authentication SDK to use standard Firebase executors.

- Fixed an issue with login state being invalid when using
anonymous sign in.
(GitHub [#3885](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/3885))

- Fixed
[`getEnrollmentTimestamp()`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/auth/MultiFactorInfo#getEnrollmentTimestamp())
in `MultiFactorInfo` to return `enrollmentTimestamp` in seconds.
(GitHub [#4001](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/4001))

#### Authentication Kotlin extensions version 22.0.0
The Kotlin extensions library transitively includes the updated
`firebase-auth` library. The Kotlin extensions library has no additional
updates.

### Cloud Firestore version 24.6.0
- Fixed stack overflow caused by deeply nested server timestamps.
(GitHub [#4702](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/4702))

- Added new
[cache config APIs](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/firestore/FirebaseFirestoreSettings.Builder#setLocalCacheSettings(com.google.firebase.firestore.LocalCacheSettings))
to customize the SDK's cache setup.

- Added
[LRU garbage collector](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/firestore/MemoryLruGcSettings)
to the SDK's memory cache.

- Deprecated the following APIs from
[`FirebaseFirestoreSettings`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/firestore/FirebaseFirestoreSettings):
`isPersistenceEnabled` and `getCacheSizeBytes`.

- Deprecated the following APIs from
[`FirebaseFirestoreSettings.Builder`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/firestore/FirebaseFirestoreSettings.Builder#setLocalCacheSettings(com.google.firebase.firestore.LocalCacheSettings)):
`isPersistenceEnabled`, `getCacheSizeBytes`, `setPersistenceEnabled`,
and `setCacheSizeBytes`.

- Internal changes to ensure alignment with other SDK releases.

#### Cloud Firestore Kotlin extensions version 24.6.0
The Kotlin extensions library transitively includes the updated
`firebase-firestore` library. The Kotlin extensions library has no additional
updates.

