### Analytics version 17.3.0
- Added support for Ecommerce

 - The following ecommerce events are added to
 [`FirebaseAnalytics.Event`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event):

 [`Event#ADD_SHIPPING_INFO`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#ADD_SHIPPING_INFO),
 [`Event#PURCHASE`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#PURCHASE),
 [`Event#REFUND`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#REFUND),
 [`Event#SELECT_ITEM`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#SELECT_ITEM),
 [`Event#SELECT_PROMOTION`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#SELECT_PROMOTION),
 [`Event#VIEW_CART`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#VIEW_CART), and
 [`Event#VIEW_PROMOTION`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#VIEW_PROMOTION)

 - The following ecommerce parameters are added to
 [`FirebaseAnalytics.Param`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param):

 [`Param#ITEMS`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEMS),
 [`Param#DISCOUNT`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#DISCOUNT),
 [`Param#ITEM_CATEGORY2`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_CATEGORY2),
 [`Param#ITEM_CATEGORY3`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_CATEGORY3),
 [`Param#ITEM_CATEGORY4`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_CATEGORY4),
 [`Param#ITEM_CATEGORY5`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_CATEGORY5),
 [`Param#ITEM_LIST_ID`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_LIST_ID),
 [`Param#ITEM_LIST_NAME`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_LIST_NAME),
 [`Param#LOCATION_ID`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#LOCATION_ID),
 [`Param#PAYMENT_TYPE`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#PAYMENT_TYPE),
 [`Param#PROMOTION_ID`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#PROMOTION_ID),
 [`Param#PROMOTION_NAME`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#PROMOTION_NAME), and
 [`Param#SHIPPING_TIER`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#SHIPPING_TIER)
- The following
[Events](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event)
are deprecated:

 - [`Event#ECOMMERCE_PURCHASE`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#ECOMMERCE_PURCHASE)
 is deprecated. Instead, use [`Event#PURCHASE`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#PURCHASE).


### Analytics version 17.3.0

 - [`Event#PURCHASE_REFUND`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#PURCHASE_REFUND)
 is deprecated. Instead, use [`Event#REFUND`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#REFUND).

 - [`Event#PRESENT_OFFER`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#PRESENT_OFFER)
 is deprecated. Instead, use [`Event#VIEW_PROMOTION`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#VIEW_PROMOTION).

 - [`Event#SELECT_CONTENT`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#SELECT_CONTENT)
 is deprecated. Instead, use [`Event#SELECT_ITEM`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#SELECT_ITEM).

 - The following events are deprecated with no replacement:
 [`Event#SET_CHECKOUT_OPTION`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#SET_CHECKOUT_OPTION),
 [`Event#CHECKOUT_PROGRESS`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#CHECKOUT_PROGRESS), and
 [`Event#VIEW_SEARCH_RESULTS`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Event#VIEW_SEARCH_RESULTS)
- The following
[Parameters](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param)
are deprecated:

 - [`Param#ITEM_LOCATION_ID`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_LOCATION_ID)
 is deprecated. Instead, use [`Param#LOCATION_ID`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#LOCATION_ID).

 - [`Param#ITEM_LIST`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_LIST)
 is deprecated. Instead, use [`Param#ITEM_LIST_NAME`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#ITEM_LIST_NAME).

 - The following parameters are deprecated with no replacement:
 [`Param#CHECKOUT_STEP`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#CHECKOUT_STEP) and
 [`Param#CHECKOUT_OPTION`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/analytics/FirebaseAnalytics.Param#CHECKOUT_OPTION)

#### Analytics Kotlin extensions version 17.3.0
- The Analytics Android library with Kotlin extensions
is now available. The Kotlin extensions library transitively includes the
base `firebase-analytics` library. To learn more, visit the
[Analytics KTX documentation](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/kotlin/com/google/firebase/analytics/ktx/package-summary).

### Cloud Firestore version 21.4.2
- Removed Guava dependency from the SDK. This change is the first
step in eliminating crashes caused by apps that depend on the wrong flavor of
Guava. ( [Issue #1125](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/1125))

#### Cloud Firestore Kotlin extensions version 21.4.2
The Kotlin extensions library transitively includes the updated
`firebase-firestore` library. The Kotlin extensions library has no additional
updates.

### Cloud Messaging version 20.1.4
- Internal changes to ensure functionality alignment with other SDK releases.

### Crashlytics version 17.0.0-beta03
- Fixed internal bugs to improve crash analysis and grouping.

- Improved compatibility with Google Analytics. For best
performance, make sure you're using the latest versions of the
Firebase Crashlytics SDK and the Firebase SDK for Google Analytics.

- Updated remaining Crashlytics backend API calls to prepare
for Fabric sunset.

### Crashlytics NDK version 17.0.0-beta03
- Updated package name in `AndroidManifest.xml` to reflect new
Firebase Crashlytics NDK package name.

- Improved debug logging.

- Released new `crashlytics.h` with updated C++ APIs.

- Added ProGuard rules files to avoid obfuscating public APIs called
from C++.

### Firebase Installations version 16.2.0
- Fixed a possible `IllegalStateException` when multiple Firebase
services required a Firebase client identifier (FID) in parallel. The
issue was not reproducible in local testing and affected a small number of
users (that is, <1%).
( [Issue #1339](https://github.com/firebase/firebase-android-sdk/issues/1339))

- Added a lint check to the compile process that prevents parallel
usage of Firebase installations and incompatible versions of the Firebase
Instance ID SDK that are older than `firebase-iid:20.1.0`.
Firebase installations creates FIDs as Firebase client identifiers.
Versions of the Firebase Instance ID SDK before `v20.1.0` created different
Firebase client identifiers: Instance IDs. This check prevents problems for
Firebase targeting that might be caused by conflicting Firebase client
identifiers.

### Firebase Instance ID version 20.1.3
- Tokens are now scoped to their respective `FirebaseApp` instance.
Apps that instantiate multiple `FirebaseApp` instances will now see a
different token for each app.

- `FirebaseApp` now requires a non-empty project ID set in the
corresponding `FirebaseOptions`.

