### Firebase Instance ID version 16.2.0
- Added the [`getInstanceId`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/iid/FirebaseInstanceId#getInstanceId())
method to [`FirebaseInstanceId`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/iid/FirebaseInstanceId#getInstanceId()).
The method returns a [`Task`](https://developers.google.com/android/reference/com/google/android/gms/tasks/Task)
that can be used to get an [`InstanceIdResult`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/iid/InstanceIdResult)
that contains the ID and token.

- Deprecated the [`getToken`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/iid/FirebaseInstanceId#getToken())
method of [`FirebaseInstanceId`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/iid/FirebaseInstanceId)
in favor of the newly-introduced [`getInstanceId`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/iid/FirebaseInstanceId#getInstanceId()).

- Deprecated the [`FirebaseInstanceIdService`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/iid/FirebaseInstanceIdService)
class in favor of overriding the `onNewToken` method of [`FirebaseMessagingService`](https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/android/com/google/firebase/messaging/FirebaseMessagingService).

